<!--
  The zones of the table: where tiles may lie, as FRACTIONS of the design view of each shape (Landscape 1280 x 720, Portrait 720 x 1280,
  Narrow 1080 x 768). The size of a tile is not written here: the solver (src/Mahjong/Table/TableSolver.h) takes the largest tile that fits
  the zone for what the rules allow it to hold, so a zone is never too small for its tiles. The comment after a zone gives it in design
  units (x y w x h) as it is after snapping to a quarter unit; the fractions are what counts. The layout is fitted to the real view
  (uniform scale, centred) afterwards. The file is read at the start and again while the game runs (edit and save, or use the Config Editor):
  a file that fails the reader or the check of the table (CheckTableLayoutSpec) is refused and the last good one stays.

  A zone is x, y, w, h, each 0..1. The seats are by screen position: 0 bottom (the viewer), 1 right, 2 top, 3 left.
    Hand, Melds, Bonus  tiles in a line; a zone wider than it is long runs along the width (a row), a taller one along the height (a column
                        of turned tiles, the side seats). The zone holds: Hand 14 tiles, Melds 4 kongs (16 tiles, a gap between melds),
                        Bonus 8 tiles. Attributes:
      align    start | center | end, where the tiles lie across the line when the zone is thicker than a tile (default start);
      spread   true to spread the hand over the zone's length instead of side by side (the viewer's hand in Portrait);
      tile     solve (default) or profile: the width is asked for by the phone profile and clamped (see Phone below);
      minTileW the smallest tile width this zone may solve to: a file that solves smaller is refused (default 0, no minimum).
    Discards            the pile of the seat: rows of 6 tiles, `rows` rows without overlap (default 5); a longer pile squeezes its rows
                        together inside the zone, so a zone never grows.
    Plate               the seat plate (152 x 80); nothing else lies on it and it keeps 4 units clear of every discard block and the wall.
    Wall                the ring of 26 x 12 stacks; the centre panel is the ring inset by one stack.
  Tile sizes follow one rule: width w, height floor(w * 4 / 3).
  A Shape with like="Name" borrows the zones (and the Free regions) of that shape and lies `inset` (a fraction of its own width) from the left
  edge (Wide).
  Free      <Free name="table.x" x y w h/>: a region of free ground in the shape, for the canvases of the table (the node files in config/nodes/
            anchor to it with region="table.x"; the names every shape must have are listed in Table/TableRegions.h). It is a place, not a
            tile zone: CheckTableLayoutSpec holds it inside the view and clear of every tile, discard block, wall ring and plate of the
            worst-case table, for every viewer and the phone profile, so a zone that moves onto a region is refused. A name is given once
            per shape and is not one of the names the table publishes from its zones (table.plate.0..3, table.centerPanel, table.wall).
  Other files rely on the Free regions, so a clearance is written next to the region (or the zone that keeps it); tests/TableLayoutTest.cpp
  holds the regions, and what the check cannot see (the Rules button of the menu) by a test of its own.
-->
<TableLayout>

